# Pretium OpenCPO workspace

- RTL-HK (Hostinger). Workspace root: `/docker/pretium-opencpo`. Same repo for all four OpenCPO chats; separate chats.
- **Solution architect** chat title: `HK/Lead/opencpo-architect` — strategy, solution design, backlog with Admin, build briefs, test direction, Tridens→OpenCPO migration design. Start: `pretiumsynergy-deploy/docs/handoffs/2026-11-14-opencpo-solution-architect-handoff.md`.
- **Dev** chat title: `HK/Dev/opencpo` — builds an approved brief, checks its own work, then offers the build to Test. Commits and deploys only after the architect has approved the build against the brief.
- **Test** chat title: `HK/Test/opencpo` — test strategy, plan and cases, as the architect directs. Signs acceptance of a feature when its test passes. Start: `pretiumsynergy-deploy/docs/handoffs/2026-11-13-opencpo-member-test-brief.md`.
- **Operations** chat title: `HK/Operations/opencpo` — runs the live system (add a charger, reports, alerts). New behaviour goes to the architect first. Pricing, tariff, visibility and billing changes need Admin approval.
- Pinned scopes: `pretiumsynergy-deploy/docs/chat-scope-pins.md`.
- Start and stop only with the three files: `docker-compose.yml`, `docker-compose.pretium.yml`, `docker-compose.traefik.yml`.
- Do not move or rename this folder. Volume names (`pretium-opencpo_pgdata`) come from it.
- Back up `pretium-opencpo_pgdata` before any upgrade, migration or `down -v`. Never run `down -v` without Admin approval.
- `cpo.` is behind Authentik (`pretium-staff`). `app.cpo.` and `ocpp.cpo.` must never get Authentik or Basic Auth: drivers and chargers use them. `ocpp.cpo` is WebSocket port 9100 only — do not publish the management API there until open reads are locked.
- `.env` is Admin-owned. Never print or edit secret values.
- Architect and Dev do not mark a feature accepted. Test owns that gate.
- Admin signs any move of a charger off Tridens. No other chat marks cutover.
- Dev and Operations do not change compose, Traefik or Authentik. That change needs the architect and Admin approval.
- Follow the mandatory cycle: Preview, Approve, Commit, Deploy by Agent, Verify, then the post-deploy resource check.
- Source CPO until cutover: `pretium-cpo.tridenstechnology.com` (Tridens white-label).
